! Inheritance (`$:/tags/hypergsd/Inheritance`)

Members run at exactly one moment: the point of creation, inside
`create-gsd-tiddler` (the new-item modal's submit). No render or refresh path
evaluates them — a member's cost is paid once per created item.

!! Contract

Each member is transcluded with these variables:

* `create-title` — the tiddler being created
* `new-type` — its GSD type
* `calling-tiddler` — the tiddler whose panel the creation came from; blank
  when invoked outside the story river (toolbar, sidebar)
* `new-data-title`, `new-state` — the modal's two temps

Tag rules send `tm-add-tag` within the surrounding fieldmangler (they render
inside the created tiddler). Field-writing rules are pointless: the pass-through
copies the data temp's render-time fields, and a rendered list's children cache,
so mid-submit temp mutation — deletion included — never reaches the copy loop.
Field values are the attribute sections' responsibility at pick time.

!! Shipped members

* `HyperGSD` — ''tag inheritance'': the caller's tags flow onto the new item,
  except `$:/`-prefixed (system) tags — type, realm and tickler families must
  never leak, and deliberate system-tag relationships ship their own rule
  instead. A blank calling-tiddler (creation outside the story river)
  inherits nothing. Users switch this off in Settings → Behaviour
  (''Inherit the tiddler's tags when creating from its panel'',
  `$:/config/hypergsd/inherit-tags`); realm and context rules are unaffected.
* `HyperGSD` — ''realm tags'': the modal's effective-realm state (NoRealm/none
  guards; a typed new-realm name wins) plus the caller's realm tags, unique.
* `HyperGSD-Contexts` — ''context tags'': the modal's picked context, the
  effective-context state and the caller's context tags, validated as
  contexts, for types that take contexts.

!! Removal

Members are plain tag scans — no list-field pinning. To disable a shipped rule,
edit it and remove its tag: the edit creates a user tiddler that supersedes the
plugin shadow (shadows cannot be deleted), and the scan stops admitting it.
Delete your tiddler and the shadow returns. Deleting the user tiddler is the
only cleanup needed; the wiki's shadow is never modified.